          "text": "{\"evidence\":[{\"paragraph_id\":\"p31\",\"quote\":\"The majority of known asteroids orbit within the asteroid belt between the orbits of Mars and Jupiter, generally in relatively low-eccentricity (i.e. not very elongated) orbits.\"},{\"paragraph_id\":\"p32\",\"quote\":\"Contrary to popular imagery, the asteroid belt is mostly empty. The asteroids are spread over such a large volume that reaching an asteroid without aiming carefully would be improbable.\"},{\"paragraph_id\":\"p33\",\"quote\":\"The four largest objects, Ceres, Vesta, Pallas, and Hygiea, account for maybe 62% of the belt's total mass, with 39% accounted for by Ceres alone.\"}]}"
